  "methodology": "Same extended scripts/benchmark.mjs against an isolated git baseline and local SDK sources on one machine. Warm, rotating case order; mean includes await and harness overhead. Core runs use 7 baseline and 9 optimized rounds; focused HTTP runs use 9 rounds each. Message bursts contain 1000 messages; HTTP bursts contain 50 requests. No external service, TLS, or competing SDK was measured. Timing differences near 1x are noise-sensitive.",
  "changes": [
    "Adopt unobserved parsed JSON as immutable message data; copy observed payloads.",
    "Clone and freeze plain data together; reuse owned immutable snapshots.",
    "Cache stable listener arrays and avoid promises for synchronous primitive results.",
    "Skip hydration for disabled caches and use one clock read per TTL sweep.",
    "Pipeline known read routes with atomic rate reservations; preserve write ordering."
  ],
